  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan treats information on Divine Bean Palace as rare even inside Shadow Sect’s true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        1520
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "house_divine_bean_palace",
        "fac_shadow_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After getting Shadow Sect’s true inheritance, Lang Ya blessed land’s land spirit exchanges most of the true inheritances’ information with Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        1540
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "exchange-with-lang-ya",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If Spectral Soul Demon Venerable had not failed and been captured by Heavenly Court, this true inheritance would not exist; after capture, with Fang Yuan as lingering hope, Spectral Soul forms Shadow Sect’s true inheritance to raise that strength.",
      "chapters": [
        1658
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_spectral_soul_demon_venerable",
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A unique soul cultivation technique recorded in Shadow Sect true inheritance lets the human soul break its limit and reach desolate soul level; Fang Yuan modifies that killer move into a more stable formation and sends his hundred million man soul through it. Those records also state that when a human soul breaks through to desolate soul, it cannot fly, because humans are innately unable to fly.",
      "chapters": [
        1804
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "desolate-soul-method",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even without Thieving Heaven’s true inheritance and Giant Sun’s true inheritance, Shadow Sect’s true inheritance contains many inheritances and records of many qi path killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        1809
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "contained-records",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_thieving_heaven_true_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan obtained Shadow Sect’s true inheritance, he did not choose to focus heavily on soul path, because Spectral Soul’s capture left that soul path true inheritance with little value and a risk that Heavenly Court could decipher and counter it.",
      "chapters": [
        1859
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-path-priority",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan has Shadow Sect’s true inheritance, and soul taker battlefield is included in it, so he knows a lot about that move.",
      "chapters": [
        2045
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-taker-battlefield",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Orderly well is a rank nine killer move from Shadow Sect’s true inheritance; it uses City Well as the core, can modify secluded domains of heaven and earth, and removes conflict between dao marks to make restoration convenient. Fang Yuan never grasps that killer move because he lacks its crucial core Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        2136
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "orderly-well",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_city_well",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    }
  ],
